@startuml
' Timing — the budget from the tab's address to the note on the screen
' Sources: ../../operations/performance.md, RNF-01, RNF-04
'
' The times are on the messages, because the ruler of a timing diagram needs a
' PlantUML newer than the one this project has.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #333
autonumber

actor "The browser" as BR
participant "The reader\n(server.py)" as SRV
participant "The workspace" as WS
participant "The file's page" as PAGE
participant "The renderer" as MD

BR -> SRV : GET /?open=<path> (0.4 ms)
activate SRV
SRV -> BR : the workspace
deactivate SRV
BR -> WS : the page runs
activate WS
WS -> SRV : GET /api/tree?path=<folder> (1.0 ms)
activate SRV
SRV -> WS : the names inside it
deactivate SRV
WS -> SRV : GET /view/<path>?embed=1 (0.7 ms)
activate SRV
SRV -> BR : the file's own page
deactivate SRV
deactivate WS
BR -> PAGE : the page runs
activate PAGE
PAGE -> SRV : GET /f/<path> (0.7 ms)
activate SRV
SRV -> PAGE : the bytes
deactivate SRV
PAGE -> MD : the source
activate MD
MD -> PAGE : the document is built
deactivate MD
deactivate PAGE
MD -> BR : the note is on the screen (90 ms in all)

note right
  90 ms measured in all, of which the reader
  answers 2 ms. The rest is the browser: the
  engine's scripts, the parse and the first
  paint. It is not measured apart yet, which is a gap
  in ../analysis/requirements.md.
end note
@enduml
